X:6
T:Banshee's Wail over the Mangle Pit, The
T:Young Tom Ennis, The
R:jig
C:Trad
N:Transcribed by Alan Ng
S:as taught by Liz Carroll at the Folklore Village '95 Irish Weekend
H:She didn't have a name for it, but then Martin Hayes happened to record it under this name on his _Under the Moon_ album. In 1997 I discovered the tune on a recording by Paddy Glackin and Robbie Hannan, who identified it as "The Young Tom Ennis", to be found in O'Neill's.
Z: id:ng-jigs-6 transcribed from tape of Liz Carroll by Alan Ng, alan@alan-ng.nospam (net), May 3, 1996
